== a shell started by cmd with a Windows-form PATH (backslashes, an empty entry, a trailing ;)
[/c/Windows/System32::/c/Windows]
no ; and no backslash in $PATH
C:/Windows/System32/whoami.exe
its child: C:/Windows/System32;C:/Windows
== an assignment in any form reads in MSYS form; a child gets forward-slash Windows form
/c/Windows/System32:/c/Windows
C:/Windows/System32;C:/Windows
/c/Windows/System32:/c/Windows
C:/Windows/System32;C:/Windows
/c/Windows/System32:/c/Windows
C:/Windows/System32;C:/Windows
/c/Windows/System32:/c/Windows
C:/Windows/System32;C:/Windows
== an empty entry stays in $PATH and never reaches a child
[/c/Windows/System32::/c/Windows:]
C:/Windows/System32;C:/Windows
[/c/Windows/System32::/c/Windows]
C:/Windows/System32;C:/Windows
== IFS=: gives the entries; a one-letter relative entry is ./A
/c/Windows/System32:./A:/c/Windows
3 entries
a folder: /c/Windows/System32
a folder: /c/Windows
== PATH=... cmd: the child gets exactly those entries, forward slashes, in whatever form they were written
D/stub;C:/Windows/System32
C:/Windows/System32;C:/Windows
C:/Windows/System32;C:/Windows
== an isolation PATH never falls back to the inherited one (kes-log's): a positive and a negative control
System32 on it: rc=0
'whoami' is not recognized as an internal or external command,
operable program or batch file.
== export -p round trip; a nested shell
declare -x PATH="/c/Windows/System32:/c/Windows"
/c/Windows/System32:/c/Windows
nested: /c/Windows/System32 /c/Windows
== a Windows program's colon-list argument: converted whole, or left as typed
/c/Windows:/c/Users -> C:/Windows;C:/Users
/c/Windows/System32 -> C:/Windows/System32
/c/Windows:rel -> /c/Windows:rel
/c/Windows: -> /c/Windows:
/c/Windows::/c/Users -> /c/Windows::/c/Users
/c/x/a:b -> /c/x/a:b
http://x/c:/d -> http://x/c:/d
